inery"><span class="enc-name">Isla refinery</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Isla refinery is an oil refinery on the Schottegat harbour of Willemstad, Curaçao, opened by Royal Dutch Shell in 1918 to process Venezuelan crude oil.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/al-islah-yemen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/al-islah-yemen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Al-Islah (Yemen)</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">Al-Islah, the Yemeni Congregation for Reform, is the main Islamist party of Yemen, founded in 1990 after unification.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/islahiye"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/islahiye.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">İslahiye</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">İslahiye is a town in Gaziantep province in southern Turkey, in a valley east of the Nur Mountains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/islam"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/islam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Islam</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Islam is a monotheistic religion founded in Arabia in the seventh century CE through the teaching of the Prophet Muhammad, centred on the Quran.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/islam-iii-giray"><span class="enc-name">Islam III Giray</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Islam III Giray was khan of Crimea from 1644 to 1654.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/islam-karimov"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/islam-karimov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Islam Kari