e Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps is a branch of Iran's armed forces founded in 1979 to protect the Islamic Republic and its revolution.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/islamic-schools-and-branches"><span class="enc-name">Islamic schools and branches</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Islamic schools and branches are the sects, schools of jurisprudence and schools of theology into which Muslims are divided.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/islamisation"><span class="enc-name">Islamisation</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Islamisation refers to the process by which societies or rulers adopt Islam and Islamic institutions, through conversion, conquest, trade or reform.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/islamism"><span class="enc-name">Islamism</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Islamism is a range of movements holding that Islam should shape politics and the state through sharia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/islamization"><span class="enc-name">Islamization</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Islamisation, also spelled Islamization, is the process by which societies adopt Islam and Islamic institutions.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/islay"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/islay.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Islay</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Islay is the southernmost island of the Inner Hebrides of Scotland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/isle-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/isle-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Isle (river)</span><span class="enc-type">Place<