enc-snip">Ismail Qemali was an Albanian statesman from Vlorë who had served as an Ottoman official and liberal deputy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ismet-inonu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ismet-inonu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">İsmet İnönü</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">İsmet İnönü was a Turkish general and statesman, Mustafa Kemal Atatürk's closest ally.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/isny-im-allgau"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/isny-im-allgau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Isny im Allgäu</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Isny im Allgäu is a town in the western Allgäu in Baden-Württemberg that grew around a Benedictine abbey founded in 1096.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/isocrates"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/isocrates.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Isocrates</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Isocrates was an Athenian orator and teacher of rhetoric.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/isokelekel"><span class="enc-name">Isokelekel</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Isokelekel is a semi-legendary hero of Pohnpei in Micronesia who, according to oral tradition, overthrew the Saudeleur dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/isonokami-shrine"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/isonokami-shrine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Isonokami Shrine</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Isonokami Shrine is a Shinto shrine in Tenri, Nara Prefecture, one of the oldest in Japan.</span></a></li><l